+prometheus-node-exporter (1.12.1-3) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  freshdeb: the defaults are upstream's now, except for the textfile
+  directory (/var/lib/prometheus/node-exporter). Debian's packages, and
+  this one up to 1.12.1-2, changed three more:
+
+   * The systemd collector is off by default, as upstream has it. To keep
+     its node_systemd_* metrics, add --collector.systemd to ARGS in
+     /etc/default/prometheus-node-exporter. It reports .target units too,
+     as upstream does (--collector.systemd.unit-exclude to change that).
+   * Filesystems mounted under /mnt, /media and /run are reported again;
+     upstream only leaves out /run/credentials. To exclude them as before:
+     --collector.filesystem.mount-points-exclude='^/(dev|proc|run|sys|mnt|media|var/lib/docker/.+|var/lib/containers/storage/.+)($|/)'
+   * Upstream's deprecated flags (--collector.netdev.device-whitelist and
+     -blacklist, --collector.systemd.unit-whitelist and -blacklist) are
+     accepted again, with a warning.
+
+ -- freshdeb <packages@freshdeb.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
+
